0,Mohegan-Pequot language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohegan-Pequot_language,"April 13, 2026 - Mohegan-Pequot (also known as Mohegan-Pequot-Montauk, Secatogue, and Shinnecock-Poosepatuck) is an Algonquian language formerly spoken, and currently being reclaimed, by the Indigenous peoples of southern present-day New England and eastern Long Island.",Mohegan-Pequot,Algic
1,Mohegan - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohegan,"May 14, 2026 - The Mohegan language is part of the Mohegan-Pequot branch of the Eastern Algonquian languages, which include the traditional languages of many Indigenous peoples along the Atlantic coast from Canada to the Chesapeake Bay. Eastern Algonquian is a subgroup of the larger Algonquian language family, itself a branch of the Algic ...",Mohegan-Pequot,Algic
